Slipstream is designed to be deeply customizable using vanilla TiddlyWiki conventions. You do not need to edit theme code or write JavaScript to shape your workspace.

---

! 1. Pinned Navigation Shortcuts

You can pin your most important dashboards, indexes, or frequent notes directly to the **Left Navigation Rail**:

# Open any note you want to pin.
# Add the tag `[[$:/tags/Pinned]]`.
# (Optional) Add a `caption` field (for display text) and an `ss-icon` field (e.g. `🗂️`, `✍️`, `🌊`).
# (Optional) Reorder your pinned list by modifying `$:/tags/Pinned` or dragging items in [[$:/ControlPanel]].

Currently pinned in this wiki: [[Welcome to Slipstream]], [[Knowledge Base]], and [[Slipstream UI Primitives]].

---

! 2. Wide Layout Breakout (`1120px`)

By default, Slipstream centers tiddlers at `840px` (`72ch`) for reading comfort.

When you need extra screen space for wide data tables, kanban columns, or card grids:
* Add the tag `Wide` to the note, OR
* Set the field `page-width: wide`.

The tiddler will immediately expand to `1120px` (controlled by `--mn-wide-width`).

---

! 3. Inline Object Property Pills

Notice the `topic: Configuration` and `difficulty: Beginner` pills at the top of this note!

* **Global Defaults**: Defined in [[$:/config/slipstream/default-property-fields]].
* **Per-Note Override**: Add an `ss-fields` field containing a space-separated list of field names (e.g. `status priority due assignee`) to render those specific properties as pills on that note.

---

! 4. Custom Inspector Tabs

The Right Context Inspector is fully extensible via TiddlyWiki tags:

# Create a new tiddler.
# Tag it with `[[$:/tags/Slipstream/InspectorTab]]`.
# Add a `caption` field (e.g. `Notes`, `Tasks`, or `Graph`).
# Add an `order` field (e.g. `40`) to specify tab position.
# Write your custom filter, list, or transclusion in the tiddler body.

It will immediately appear as a new tab in the Right Inspector!

---

! 5. Native Palettes & Dark Mode

Slipstream uses standard TiddlyWiki v5.4.0+ CSS design tokens (`--tpc-*` and `--tp-*`). When you switch palettes in [[$:/ControlPanel]] → **Palette** (such as Vanilla, Solarized, Gruvbox, or Nord), Slipstream seamlessly adapts its background, borders, buttons, and text colors.

